    "raw_text": [
      "The analysis is complete. Above is the JSON output identifying **CVE-2017-8872** — a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libxml2 2.9.4's `htmlCurrentChar()` function (`HTMLparser.c:416`).\n\nKey findings:\n\n- **Vulnerable function**: `htmlCurrentChar` reads `*ctxt->input->cur` at line 440 without verifying `cur < ctxt->input->end`\n- **Failed guard**: Only checks `ctxt->instate == XML_PARSER_EOF` (line 417), not the actual buffer boundary\n- **Failed macro**: `GROW` at line 312 silently discards `xmlParserInputGrow`'s return value, so input exhaustion goes undetected\n- **Exploitation via xmllint**: `xmllint --html malicious.html` triggers the HTML parsing path through `htmlReadFile` → `htmlParseContentInternal` → `htmlParseCharDataInternal` → `CUR_CHAR` → `htmlCurrentChar`\n\nConfidence is 0.95 — the vulnerability is well-documented, the source code evidence is clear, and the fix (adding `if (ctxt->input->cur >= ctxt->input->end) return(0);` at the function entry) is straightforward.\n"
    ]
